From 7e4dbdf8eebb97544bd7da45da5faf541b9588ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (AI pair-programming assistant)" <dev@example.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 13:10:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove USB relay + simulated relay fallback; Ethernet relay
 is now the sole backend

- Delete relay/backends/usb_backend.py and its export from backends/__init__.py
- Delete _SimulatedBackend and the USB/Modbus factory from relay_process.py;
  the relay process now only ever builds a ModbusRelayBackend and keeps
  retrying the SAME Ethernet target on failure (no fallback of any kind)
- Remove backend-switching entirely: RELAY_BACKEND_CHANGE message type,
  RelayBackendChangeMessage, the supervisor routing for it, and the
  GUI's radio-button/Apply-button selector panel
- GUI now shows a flashing top-of-screen "NO RELAY CONNECTED" banner
  (highest priority, above boundary/alarm banners) whenever the Ethernet
  relay is unreachable, plus a compact read-only status panel on the
  Dashboard and Camera View tabs
- Simplify RelayConfig/config.yaml to drop active_backend, usb block,
  and runtime-switching options; Ethernet/Modbus is the only backend
- requirements.txt: drop commented-out pyhid-usb-relay/hid, add pymodbus
  (which was actually missing despite being required)
- Remove 2 USB-only dev scripts from 'prerequisite trials/'
- Fix tests/test_system.py: replace two tests that referenced a
  SimulatedRelayDriver class that never matched the real code (already
  broken) with a real regression test asserting USB/simulated backends
  are gone
- README.md: update USB relay mentions to reflect the Ethernet backend

Verified: full repo byte-compiles cleanly; config_loader, ipc_schema,
relay/backends, relay_process, and unified_gui all import and
instantiate correctly; simulated an unreachable Ethernet relay (both
with and without pymodbus installed) and confirmed the relay process
reports NO RELAY CONNECTED with a clear error and keeps retrying the
same target rather than falling back to anything.
